<title>SWITZERLAND: Management buyout at Ascom Zeag unit.</title>
<headline>Management buyout at Ascom Zeag unit.</headline>
<dateline>BERNE 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss telecommunications group Ascom Holding AG said it had sold its Ascom Zeag AG unit in a management buyout that took effect on January 1, 1997.</p>
<p>Ascom said in a statement that from March 1 the company, which develops, manufacturers and distributes carpark management systems, would operate under the name of Zeag Parking AG.</p>
<p>Zeag is headquartered in Spreitenbach, near Zurich, and employs some 40 people.</p>
<p>Besides management, the buyout involves Diethelm &amp; Co. AG of Zurich and Zuehlke Engineering AG of Schlieren.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
